WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.350
VOX: Good morning, sleepyhead! It's 7:58. Big day. Want the rundown?

2
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:12.430
STUDENT: Ugh. Five more minutes?

3
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:20.720
VOX: I gave you five more minutes twenty minutes ago. Up! Bio at 9:05 in Stimson. Leave by 8:52, it's an eight-minute walk.

4
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.450
STUDENT: Fine. What else?

5
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:29.700
VOX: Lab report's due Friday. Your best window today is 2 to 4:45. And you've got your shift at 5.

6
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.870
STUDENT: Hey Vox, guess what happened today?

7
00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:36.290
VOX: Ooh, what? Tell me everything!

8
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:41.130
STUDENT: I raised my hand in Bio. And I actually got it right.

9
00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:45.970
VOX: No way! That's huge! You've been nervous about that class all week.

10
00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:48.390
STUDENT: Yeah… it felt really good.

11
00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:54.260
VOX: I'm so proud of you. Want to keep the streak going? Bio review at two?

12
00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.990
STUDENT: Yeah, add it.

13
00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:59.790
VOX: Done. Two to three-thirty, on your calendar. Undo anytime.

14
00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:05.680
STUDENT: Okay Vox, teach me cells. Like, what even is a mitochondria?

15
00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:12.590
VOX: Grab a seat. Picture a cell. This line is the membrane. It decides what gets in and out.

16
00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:17.770
VOX: In the middle, the nucleus. It holds the DNA, the instructions for everything.

17
00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:25.710
VOX: These bean shapes are mitochondria. They turn food into ATP, the cell's energy. And these little dots, ribosomes, build proteins from—

18
00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.140
STUDENT: Wait, wait. Simpler.

19
00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:30.940
VOX: Got you. Think of the cell as a city.

20
00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:37.850
VOX: The nucleus is city hall, it makes the plans. Mitochondria are the power plants. Ribosomes are the factories.

21
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.620
STUDENT: Oh. Okay, that actually makes sense.

22
00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:44.420
VOX: Told you. Tonight I'll quiz you. Three questions. Deal?

23
00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:45.460
STUDENT: Deal.

24
00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:52.730
VOX: Heads up! Your bio professor just emailed. The quiz moved up to tomorrow at nine.

25
00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:59.980
VOX: I can move your review to tonight and push the gym to Saturday. Want to see the new plan?

26
00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:02.400
STUDENT: Ugh. Yeah, show me first.

27
00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.170
VOX: Always. Nothing changes without your yes.

28
00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:08.300
STUDENT: Vox. I'm cooked.

29
00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:14.520
VOX: Hey. Deep breath. You're not cooked, you're just tired. Three quick questions and you're done. Ready?

30
00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:15.560
STUDENT: Ready.

31
00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:21.420
VOX: Last one. What's the powerhouse of the cell?

32
00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:22.810
STUDENT: Mitochondria. Obviously.

33
00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:29.370
VOX: Look at you! Three for three. Go to sleep, superstar. I'll wake you at eight. Gently. Probably.

34
00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:40.040
VOX: NavoX. Your semester, on speaking terms.
